implementationPlan.description:
1. Implement read-only board tree construction with tests first (DoD 1–2,4). After WT-11 lands, add new self-contained `board_snapshot CONTROL_TOP TASK_ID STATUS` / `Invoke-MoeBoardSnapshot -Top ... -TaskId ... -Status ...`, using the same small inline Node program in both wrappers (node stdin script, values in argv; never splice values into executable source). Existing Node is already required; avoid a new asset/manifest. Worktree-mode control root must be the verified repository root, never W; no nested-project support is added. Use a private temp directory/index OUTSIDE .moe, child-process argv arrays, and Git env with inherited GIT_INDEX_FILE/GIT_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE/GIT_COMMON_DIR removed and only the owned GIT_INDEX_FILE set. Read refs/moe/board: genuine absent ref => empty index; existing ref must resolve to a valid commit, other Git errors => skip. Seed temp index from old tree, not main. Allow only regular `.moe/tasks/*.json`, `.moe/epics/*.json`, `.moe/project.json` (flat canonical daemon records); never runtime subdirectories, non-JSON files, symlink/junction escapes or an unexpected non-board parent-tree entry. Read each file to a Buffer once, validate UTF-8/JSON from that captured content, then persist exactly that Buffer to an owned temp copy for Git hashing. Never parse then git-add the mutable source. Invalid/unreadable/changed-during-read files keep their old index entry (new invalid files remain absent), with a bounded escaped log naming each path; do not log content. Refuse/retain unsafe links, checking the input directories too. Confirmed deletions absent from a successfully enumerated directory and still missing at recheck remove only that prior index entry; ENOENT after a file was enumerated is a raced read, so retain it. Directory read failure skips the snapshot rather than deleting an entire subtree. Hash captured temp copies with `git hash-object -w --no-filters -- <args>` in modest argv batches (e.g. 32 paths for Windows command-line bounds), then update the private index with NUL-delimited index-info; board files use 100644. Example invariant:
```js
const bytes = fs.readFileSync(file);
JSON.parse(new TextDecoder('utf-8', { fatal: true }).decode(bytes));
// Only bytes captured above may be hashed, never a second read of file.
```
Twin helper-level tests prove valid full board + byte-exact Unicode/CRLF content, invalid old/new JSON behavior, no external/runtime paths, confirmed deletion vs failed directory/read, and unchanged control index plus recursive .moe content/mtime signatures. Run read-only assertions around the snapshot helper itself, not around fake-daemon RPCs that legitimately mutate fixture state.
